    "terminal_reason": "completed",
    "result_text": "I've implemented `build_context` in `app/context.py` and added tests in `tests/test_context.py`. All 7 tests pass (4 existing, 3 new).\n\n**How it works:**\n- **Lookup:** it calls `retriever.invoke(question, config={\"tags\": [TRACE_TAG]})`. That's the standard way to call any LangChain retriever, so it works for both `KeywordRetriever` and a vector-store retriever, and the `kb-context` tag appears on the retriever run in traces.\n- **Selecting entries:** it goes through the documents in the order the retriever returned them. It skips any document whose `metadata[\"source\"]` has already been used, and stops once it has `MAX_SOURCES` entries.\n- **Format:** each entry is `\"[n] <source>\"`, a newline, then the document text with surrounding whitespace removed. Entries are joined with one blank line, and the result is `\"\"` if nothing was found.\n\n**New tests:**\n- Repeated sources are skipped, the numbering and format are right, and only `MAX_SOURCES` entries are returned.\n- Nothing found gives an empty string.\n- A callback handler confirms that `TRACE_TAG` reaches the retriever run.\n\nNo dependencies were added. One behaviour to know: a document with no `source` in its metadata is not skipped. It's labelled `[n] None`, and any later documents without a source are skipped as repeats of it."
